      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Think of your arteries like plumbing pipes; when high LDL levels are present, the particles can infiltrate the inner lining of these pipes. It's a slow, insidious process where the immune system mistakes the trapped LDL for invaders, creating inflammation around the plaque. This infiltration and subsequent inflammation is how the damage slowly creeps into and hardens the artery walls over time.",
